// spec: std::variant's functions and members on a typed union (`holdsAlternative<int>(v)`, `get<int>(v)`, `v.index()`, `v.get<1>()`) are errors that say how a `union enum` is asked (`v == U::Name`, v.tag()) and read (`v[Name]`), design.md 8.5; until 2026-11-06 codegen's "a call that did not resolve" or "a member access that did not resolve" (E's report)
// error: typed_union_variant_api_is_error.kpp:12: error: holdsAlternative takes no typed union (Value): a `union enum` is asked with `v == Value::Name` (or v.tag()) and read with `v[Name]` (design.md 8.5)
// error: typed_union_variant_api_is_error.kpp:13: error: get takes no typed union (Value): a `union enum` is asked with `v == Value::Name` (or v.tag()) and read with `v[Name]` (design.md 8.5)
// error: typed_union_variant_api_is_error.kpp:14: error: index is no member of the typed union Value: a `union enum` is asked with `v == Value::Name` (or v.tag()) and read with `v[Name]` (design.md 8.5)
// error: typed_union_variant_api_is_error.kpp:15: error: get is no member of the typed union Value: a `union enum` is asked with `v == Value::Name` (or v.tag()) and read with `v[Name]` (design.md 8.5)
union enum Value : u8
{
  { {int, Integer}, {double, Real} }
};
int ask(Value v)
{
  bool held = holdsAlternative<int>(v);
  int value = get<int>(v);
  int which = v.index();
  int second = v.get<1>();
  return held ? value + which + second : 0;
}
int main()
{
  Value v;
  v[Integer] = 5;
  return v == Value::Integer ? v[Integer] - 5 : 1;
}
